{"parentUuid":"347a4ac9-d010-4240-8872-6b368e45b863","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfNku4YVDJbPqaeAgLich","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01JBynFEuKsM7Ede2brEjgWL","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/Users/vojta/.claude/projects/-Users-vojta-Dev-protocodus-github-io/memory/alpen-debug-workflow.md"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4719,"cache_read_input_tokens":140160,"output_tokens":1583,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1330},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4719,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1583,"cache_read_input_tokens":140160,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4719,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4719},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[{"type":"thinking_dropped","path":"messages.2.content.0","reason":"prefix_binding_mismatch"}],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01JBynFEuKsM7Ede2brEjgWL":{"file_path":"/Users/vojta/.claude/projects/-Users-vojta-Dev-protocodus-github-io/memory/alpen-debug-workflow.md"}},"apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CfNktzHk3GKnBeaK3zHNb","type":"assistant","uuid":"65f82676-48e0-4ecb-a311-072fbc629d85","timestamp":"2026-09-24T18:43:50.377Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"max","perTurnEffort":"max","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"REDACTED","sessionId":"f31fbc8b-fac8-4283-8f36-bb5424b19347","version":"2.1.281","gitBranch":"main","slug":"enchanted-prancing-stroustrup"}
{"parentUuid":"65f82676-48e0-4ecb-a311-072fbc629d85","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"2be28adf-05f1-4bb1-a22c-bd4cd738bbc6","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01JBynFEuKsM7Ede2brEjgWL","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tname: alpen-debug-workflow\n3\tdescription: \"How to run, drive and verify the Alpen snowboarding game (fun/alpen) in a headless browser session\"\n4\tmetadata: \n5\t  node_type: memory\n6\t  type: project\n7\t  originSessionId: 122db08e-5f2c-4b4f-b5dd-8cbf6a8d18f1\n8\t  modified: 2026-09-24T14:37:27.356Z\n9\t---\n10\t\n11\tAlpen (fun/alpen) must be served from the **repo root** (protocodus.github.io), not the game dir — index.html imports three.js via the absolute path `/assets/vendor/three/three.module.min.js`. `python3 -m http.server <port>` from the root works. Vendored three is r185; GLTFLoader + utils live under fun/alpen/assets/vendor|utils.\n12\t\n13\tVerification hatches (as of 2026-08-07):\n14\t- `?seed=<code>` pins the mountain; the game writes the generated seed back into the URL.\n15\t- `window.__alpen.debug()` returns a full state snapshot; `__alpen.rider/game/scene/...` expose live objects. `debug().speed` is roughly HUD km/h × 4.35.\n16\t- `__alpen.weather.pin(tod)` freezes time-of-day (~0.35 bright morning, 0.6–0.7 golden hour, 0.93+ aurora); conditions are NOT tod-driven — loop `__alpen.weather.update(10)` until `state.storm` is where you want it. Storms rebuild over time, re-clear before beauty shots.\n17\t- Drive by dispatching KeyboardEvents on `window` (Enter starts; A/D carve, W tuck, S brake, Space pop, R restart-at-last-gate, Escape pause). **Always send matching keyup** — a keydown-only S latches the brake at 1 and the rider stands still forever.\n18\t- Probing terrain: `import('/fun/alpen/js/terrain.js')` in-page gives `guideAt(z)` (racing-line x), `gateSlotsIn(zLo,zHi)`, `rockBandAt(z)` (zone widths), `getTerrainMaterialAt(x,z)` ({groomed,powder,rock,ice}), `corridorHalfAt`, `nearestCenter`. Downhill is **−z**.\n19\t- **Never mutate `rider.pos`/`vel` from evaluate scripts** — the render half of `frame()` swaps pos/yaw for interpolation and restores them, so external writes race and corrupt state (rider flung at 200+). Use the R-restart path instead; spawns snap to `guideAt`.\n20\t- **Zero-input drift is a real regression signal, not noise — test it, don't wave it off.** Protocol: reset, send zero input, sample `pos` + `corridorHalfAt`/`nearestCenter` from terrain.js once or twice a second for 25-30s. Do this after any change to `TERRAIN.corridor`/`TERRAIN.guide`, the off-piste octave masking, **or any yaw rule in `groundStep`**.\n21\t  - **Judge the shape, not an absolute number.** A previous version of this memory claimed the fix of 2026-08-07 left drift at \"single digits to low teens of metres over 30s\". That was wrong — measured on 2026-08-07 across 5 seeds × 4 start points it was 80–156 m, and in the live browser too. Correct pass criterion: **bounded and oscillating** (offset crosses back through zero, yaw stays within a few degrees) rather than **monotonic** (offset and yaw grow together without ever turning back). A passive rider legitimately ends tens of metres off-centre because the piste's own centre line wanders away from anyone riding straight; that is not the bug. Yaw sweeping 0°→67° with no input is.\n22\t  - The real cause found on 2026-08-07 was **not** terrain: the self-centring rule in `rider.js` compared `atan2(vel.x,-vel.z)` (world horizontal bearing) against `this.yaw`, while the velocity is rebuilt along `h` — the heading *projected onto the slope*, which has a different bearing on any cross-slope. The rule read that projection as steering error and removed it, enlarging it: positive feedback at up to 11°/s. Fixed by using `atan2(vLat, vFwd)` (the slip angle, in the board's own tangent frame). Beware this class generally — **any rule comparing raw `yaw` against a world-space travel bearing has the same latent bug**; the clamps (`limitCourseYaw`, the skid clamp) only avoid it because they are thresholds, not followers.\n23\t- Fork-closing zones (two branches converging back to one) are the one case this drift check doesn't cleanly promise — a passive rider can pick up real excursion there since the \"correct\" line itself sweeps fast. Observed self-correcting rather than diverging; not worth over-tuning against since real players always steer.\n24\t\n25\t**Prefer a headless Node harness over the browser for anything about physics, handling or input.** `rider.js`, `terrain.js`, `config.js`, `noise.js` and `shadow-cache.js` import nothing from three — `rider.js` needs only a `Vector3`, so a ~40-line shim (`set/copy/add/addScaledVector/multiplyScalar/dot/cross/normalize/length/lengthSq/lerp`) plus `world = {height: heightAt, surfaceAt: getTerrainMaterialAt, canStall, beyond: beyondLipAt, grip:1, surfaceDrag:1}` runs the real 120 Hz loop in node from a `.mjs` with absolute import paths. Verified 2026-08-07: `heightAt/guideAt/nearestCenter/corridorHalfAt` match the browser digit-for-digit, so the mountain is purely procedural and the harness is faithful. This turns a flaky 30-second browser observation into a deterministic sweep over seeds × start points in under a second, and lets you instrument the rider by `sed`-copying `rider.js` into scratch and patching probes in. `input.js` also runs in node with a tiny `window` EventTarget + `KeyboardEvent` shim, which is how the display-rate jump bug was pinned down. Use the browser only for what actually needs a GPU: rendering, materials, shaders, screenshots.\n26\t\n27\tBrowser harness: both the Chrome DevTools MCP browser and the Playwright MCP browser have died mid-session under long WebGL runs here (\"Target closed\" / target-page-closed) — neither is reliably stable for a long verification session. Expect to re-navigate and lose in-page state; keep test scripts short and self-contained (reset + sample + return) rather than relying on continuing a prior page's state across tool calls. Playwright screenshots land in `.playwright-mcp/` or the CWD — delete them before committing.\n28\t\n29\t**What worked instead (2026-09-24): standalone Playwright `.mjs` scripts in the scratchpad**, run with `node` and `dangerouslyDisableSandbox` (Chrome can't launch sandboxed): `chromium.launch({ channel: 'chrome', headless: true, args: ['--use-angle=metal', '--enable-gpu', '--ignore-gpu-blocklist'] })` from `/Users/vojta/Dev/evangelist-exchange/node_modules/playwright/index.mjs` (see [[ashline-dev-workflow]]). One launch per scenario never died over dozens of runs, gets a real GPU, and `EXT_disjoint_timer_query` works, so `debug().performance.gpuMs` is live. Useful pieces: a steering autopilot dispatching A/D keydown/keyup from `setInterval` toward `guideAt(z-30)`; freezing with `__alpen.game.mode='paused'` then posing `__alpen.camera` and calling `shading.update(weather.state, camera, 0, NaN); retro.render(scene, camera)` for exact beauty shots; `__alpen.flicker.hideRelief/hideTerrain` or toggling `sky.group` children by name for layer A/Bs. For before/after perf: `git archive HEAD fun/alpen assets/vendor assets/images | tar -x -C $TMPDIR/alpen-base` and serve it on a second port; fixed camera pose + `freezeResolution`, alternate base/new runs — GPU p50 noise is ±0.5 ms on this machine, so single runs prove nothing.\n30\t\n31\t**Beware stale ES-module caches** when files change on disk mid-session: a plain reload keeps old modules, and the Playwright MCP exposes no ignore-cache reload. The reliable dodge is to **start `python3 -m http.server` on a fresh port and navigate there** — a new origin has no cache. Symptom to watch for: `TypeError: <newFn> is not a function` spamming from `frame()` while the file on disk plainly has it. Verify with `curl -s localhost:<port>/fun/alpen/js/<file>.js | grep <marker>` before blaming the code.\n32\t"}]},"uuid":"58f3bb2a-725d-4a56-81f6-96c03b74ebd2","timestamp":"2026-09-24T18:43:50.392Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/vojta/.claude/projects/-Users-vojta-Dev-protocodus-github-io/memory/alpen-debug-workflow.md","content":"---\nname: alpen-debug-workflow\ndescription: \"How to run, drive and verify the Alpen snowboarding game (fun/alpen) in a headless browser session\"\nmetadata: \n  node_type: memory\n  type: project\n  originSessionId: 122db08e-5f2c-4b4f-b5dd-8cbf6a8d18f1\n  modified: 2026-09-24T14:37:27.356Z\n---\n\nAlpen (fun/alpen) must be served from the **repo root** (protocodus.github.io), not the game dir — index.html imports three.js via the absolute path `/assets/vendor/three/three.module.min.js`. `python3 -m http.server <port>` from the root works. Vendored three is r185; GLTFLoader + utils live under fun/alpen/assets/vendor|utils.\n\nVerification hatches (as of 2026-08-07):\n- `?seed=<code>` pins the mountain; the game writes the generated seed back into the URL.\n- `window.__alpen.debug()` returns a full state snapshot; `__alpen.rider/game/scene/...` expose live objects. `debug().speed` is roughly HUD km/h × 4.35.\n- `__alpen.weather.pin(tod)` freezes time-of-day (~0.35 bright morning, 0.6–0.7 golden hour, 0.93+ aurora); conditions are NOT tod-driven — loop `__alpen.weather.update(10)` until `state.storm` is where you want it. Storms rebuild over time, re-clear before beauty shots.\n- Drive by dispatching KeyboardEvents on `window` (Enter starts; A/D carve, W tuck, S brake, Space pop, R restart-at-last-gate, Escape pause). **Always send matching keyup** — a keydown-only S latches the brake at 1 and the rider stands still forever.\n- Probing terrain: `import('/fun/alpen/js/terrain.js')` in-page gives `guideAt(z)` (racing-line x), `gateSlotsIn(zLo,zHi)`, `rockBandAt(z)` (zone widths), `getTerrainMaterialAt(x,z)` ({groomed,powder,rock,ice}), `corridorHalfAt`, `nearestCenter`. Downhill is **−z**.\n- **Never mutate `rider.pos`/`vel` from evaluate scripts** — the render half of `frame()` swaps pos/yaw for interpolation and restores them, so external writes race and corrupt state (rider flung at 200+). Use the R-restart path instead; spawns snap to `guideAt`.\n- **Zero-input drift is a real regression signal, not noise — test it, don't wave it off.** Protocol: reset, send zero input, sample `pos` + `corridorHalfAt`/`nearestCenter` from terrain.js once or twice a second for 25-30s. Do this after any change to `TERRAIN.corridor`/`TERRAIN.guide`, the off-piste octave masking, **or any yaw rule in `groundStep`**.\n  - **Judge the shape, not an absolute number.** A previous version of this memory claimed the fix of 2026-08-07 left drift at \"single digits to low teens of metres over 30s\". That was wrong — measured on 2026-08-07 across 5 seeds × 4 start points it was 80–156 m, and in the live browser too. Correct pass criterion: **bounded and oscillating** (offset crosses back through zero, yaw stays within a few degrees) rather than **monotonic** (offset and yaw grow together without ever turning back). A passive rider legitimately ends tens of metres off-centre because the piste's own centre line wanders away from anyone riding straight; that is not the bug. Yaw sweeping 0°→67° with no input is.\n  - The real cause found on 2026-08-07 was **not** terrain: the self-centring rule in `rider.js` compared `atan2(vel.x,-vel.z)` (world horizontal bearing) against `this.yaw`, while the velocity is rebuilt along `h` — the heading *projected onto the slope*, which has a different bearing on any cross-slope. The rule read that projection as steering error and removed it, enlarging it: positive feedback at up to 11°/s. Fixed by using `atan2(vLat, vFwd)` (the slip angle, in the board's own tangent frame). Beware this class generally — **any rule comparing raw `yaw` against a world-space travel bearing has the same latent bug**; the clamps (`limitCourseYaw`, the skid clamp) only avoid it because they are thresholds, not followers.\n- Fork-closing zones (two branches converging back to one) are the one case this drift check doesn't cleanly promise — a passive rider can pick up real excursion there since the \"correct\" line itself sweeps fast. Observed self-correcting rather than diverging; not worth over-tuning against since real players always steer.\n\n**Prefer a headless Node harness over the browser for anything about physics, handling or input.** `rider.js`, `terrain.js`, `config.js`, `noise.js` and `shadow-cache.js` import nothing from three — `rider.js` needs only a `Vector3`, so a ~40-line shim (`set/copy/add/addScaledVector/multiplyScalar/dot/cross/normalize/length/lengthSq/lerp`) plus `world = {height: heightAt, surfaceAt: getTerrainMaterialAt, canStall, beyond: beyondLipAt, grip:1, surfaceDrag:1}` runs the real 120 Hz loop in node from a `.mjs` with absolute import paths. Verified 2026-08-07: `heightAt/guideAt/nearestCenter/corridorHalfAt` match the browser digit-for-digit, so the mountain is purely procedural and the harness is faithful. This turns a flaky 30-second browser observation into a deterministic sweep over seeds × start points in under a second, and lets you instrument the rider by `sed`-copying `rider.js` into scratch and patching probes in. `input.js` also runs in node with a tiny `window` EventTarget + `KeyboardEvent` shim, which is how the display-rate jump bug was pinned down. Use the browser only for what actually needs a GPU: rendering, materials, shaders, screenshots.\n\nBrowser harness: both the Chrome DevTools MCP browser and the Playwright MCP browser have died mid-session under long WebGL runs here (\"Target closed\" / target-page-closed) — neither is reliably stable for a long verification session. Expect to re-navigate and lose in-page state; keep test scripts short and self-contained (reset + sample + return) rather than relying on continuing a prior page's state across tool calls. Playwright screenshots land in `.playwright-mcp/` or the CWD — delete them before committing.\n\n**What worked instead (2026-09-24): standalone Playwright `.mjs` scripts in the scratchpad**, run with `node` and `dangerouslyDisableSandbox` (Chrome can't launch sandboxed): `chromium.launch({ channel: 'chrome', headless: true, args: ['--use-angle=metal', '--enable-gpu', '--ignore-gpu-blocklist'] })` from `/Users/vojta/Dev/evangelist-exchange/node_modules/playwright/index.mjs` (see [[ashline-dev-workflow]]). One launch per scenario never died over dozens of runs, gets a real GPU, and `EXT_disjoint_timer_query` works, so `debug().performance.gpuMs` is live. Useful pieces: a steering autopilot dispatching A/D keydown/keyup from `setInterval` toward `guideAt(z-30)`; freezing with `__alpen.game.mode='paused'` then posing `__alpen.camera` and calling `shading.update(weather.state, camera, 0, NaN); retro.render(scene, camera)` for exact beauty shots; `__alpen.flicker.hideRelief/hideTerrain` or toggling `sky.group` children by name for layer A/Bs. For before/after perf: `git archive HEAD fun/alpen assets/vendor assets/images | tar -x -C $TMPDIR/alpen-base` and serve it on a second port; fixed camera pose + `freezeResolution`, alternate base/new runs — GPU p50 noise is ±0.5 ms on this machine, so single runs prove nothing.\n\n**Beware stale ES-module caches** when files change on disk mid-session: a plain reload keeps old modules, and the Playwright MCP exposes no ignore-cache reload. The reliable dodge is to **start `python3 -m http.server` on a fresh port and navigate there** — a new origin has no cache. Symptom to watch for: `TypeError: <newFn> is not a function` spamming from `frame()` while the file on disk plainly has it. Verify with `curl -s localhost:<port>/fun/alpen/js/<file>.js | grep <marker>` before blaming the code.\n","numLines":32,"startLine":1,"totalLines":32}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"65f82676-48e0-4ecb-a311-072fbc629d85","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"REDACTED","sessionId":"f31fbc8b-fac8-4283-8f36-bb5424b19347","version":"2.1.281","gitBranch":"main","slug":"enchanted-prancing-stroustrup"}
{"parentUuid":"58f3bb2a-725d-4a56-81f6-96c03b74ebd2","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfNku4YVDJbPqaeAgLich","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01SyXswFJ4GEZ8toBEse9K7r","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cat closeup.mjs | head -80","description":"Read the earlier close-up script"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4719,"cache_read_input_tokens":140160,"output_tokens":1583,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1330},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4719,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1583,"cache_read_input_tokens":140160,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4719,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4719},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[{"type":"thinking_dropped","path":"messages.2.content.0","reason":"prefix_binding_mismatch"}],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01SyXswFJ4GEZ8toBEse9K7r":{"command":"cd REDACTED && cat closeup.mjs | head -80","description":"Read the earlier close-up script"}},"wireIngestContext":{"toolu_01SyXswFJ4GEZ8toBEse9K7r":{"cwd":"REDACTED"}},"apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011CfNktzHk3GKnBeaK3zHNb","type":"assistant","uuid":"f6897b46-6ebf-4d28-bffa-ec0b0b6bb315","timestamp":"2026-09-24T18:43:51.950Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"max","perTurnEffort":"max","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"REDACTED","sessionId":"f31fbc8b-fac8-4283-8f36-bb5424b19347","version":"2.1.281","gitBranch":"main","slug":"enchanted-prancing-stroustrup"}
{"parentUuid":"f6897b46-6ebf-4d28-bffa-ec0b0b6bb315","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"2be28adf-05f1-4bb1-a22c-bd4cd738bbc6","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01SyXswFJ4GEZ8toBEse9K7r","type":"tool_result","content":"// Usage: node closeup.mjs <port> <label> [tod] [seed] [rideMs]\nimport { chromium } from '/Users/vojta/Dev/evangelist-exchange/node_modules/playwright/index.mjs';\nconst [port = '8141', label = 'base', tod = '0.42', seed = 'alpine-review', rideMs = '6000'] = process.argv.slice(2);\nconst OUT = 'REDACTED';\nconst browser = await chromium.launch({ channel: 'chrome', headless: true, args: ['--use-angle=metal', '--enable-gpu', '--ignore-gpu-blocklist'] });\nconst page = await browser.newPage({ viewport: { width: 1440, height: 900 } });\nconst logs = [];\npage.on('console', (m) => { if (m.type() === 'error' || m.type() === 'warning') logs.push(m.type() + ': ' + m.text()); });\npage.on('pageerror', (e) => logs.push('pageerror: ' + e.message));\nawait page.goto(`http://127.0.0.1:${port}/fun/alpen/?seed=${seed}`);\nawait page.waitForFunction(() => document.body.classList.contains('ready'), null, { timeout: 60000 });\nawait page.evaluate(() => window.dispatchEvent(new KeyboardEvent('keydown', { code: 'Enter', key: 'Enter' })));\nawait page.evaluate((t) => __alpen.weather.pin(+t), tod);\nawait page.evaluate(async () => {\n  const T = await import('/fun/alpen/js/terrain.js');\n  window.__pilot = setInterval(() => {\n    const r = __alpen.rider;\n    const target = T.guideAt(r.pos.z - 30);\n    const heading = Math.atan2(r.vel.x, -r.vel.z);\n    const want = Math.atan2(target - r.pos.x, 30) - heading;\n    const fire = (code, down) => window.dispatchEvent(new KeyboardEvent(down ? 'keydown' : 'keyup', { code, key: code }));\n    const left = want < -0.05, right = want > 0.05;\n    if (left !== window.__L) { fire('KeyA', left); window.__L = left; }\n    if (right !== window.__R) { fire('KeyD', right); window.__R = right; }\n  }, 50);\n});\nawait page.waitForTimeout(+rideMs);\n// freeze and hide overlays\nawait page.evaluate(() => { clearInterval(window.__pilot); __alpen.game.mode = 'paused';\n  document.querySelector('.hud').style.visibility = 'hidden'; document.querySelector('.pad').style.visibility = 'hidden'; });\nawait page.waitForTimeout(300);\nawait page.screenshot({ path: `${OUT}/${label}-freeze.png` });\nconst views = [\n  { name: 'rider-side', f: (r) => ({ eye: [r.pos.x + r.right.x * 2.6 - r.heading.x * 1.2, r.pos.y + 1.3, r.pos.z + r.right.z * 2.6 - r.heading.z * 1.2], at: [r.pos.x, r.pos.y + 0.8, r.pos.z] }) },\n  { name: 'rider-front', f: (r) => ({ eye: [r.pos.x + r.heading.x * 3.2, r.pos.y + 1.4, r.pos.z + r.heading.z * 3.2], at: [r.pos.x, r.pos.y + 0.9, r.pos.z] }) },\n  { name: 'forest', f: (r) => ({ eye: [r.pos.x, r.pos.y + 1.6, r.pos.z], at: [r.pos.x - 40, r.pos.y - 4, r.pos.z - 30] }) },\n  { name: 'forest-r', f: (r) => ({ eye: [r.pos.x, r.pos.y + 1.6, r.pos.z], at: [r.pos.x + 40, r.pos.y - 4, r.pos.z - 30] }) },\n  { name: 'back', f: (r) => ({ eye: [r.pos.x, r.pos.y + 2.0, r.pos.z - 4], at: [r.pos.x, r.pos.y + 1, r.pos.z + 20] }) },\n];\nfor (const v of views) {\n  await page.evaluate((src) => {\n    const f = eval(src);\n    const { camera, rider, shading, weather, retro, scene } = __alpen;\n    const { eye, at } = f(rider);\n    camera.position.set(...eye);\n    camera.lookAt(...at);\n    camera.fov = 60; camera.updateProjectionMatrix();\n    camera.updateMatrixWorld();\n    shading.update(weather.state, camera, 0, NaN);\n    retro.render(scene, camera);\n  }, v.f.toString());\n  await page.waitForTimeout(150);\n  await page.screenshot({ path: `${OUT}/${label}-${v.name}.png` });\n}\nconsole.log(logs.slice(0, 20).join('\\n'));\nawait browser.close();","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"d414b9ae-0be8-47b6-bcd5-be5ee4d0fefc","timestamp":"2026-09-24T18:43:52.048Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"// Usage: node closeup.mjs <port> <label> [tod] [seed] [rideMs]\nimport { chromium } from '/