{"parentUuid":"50110d64-0343-4487-862c-4286d12a4614","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"ceb8e0f6-5536-44b3-b6df-e35573bca6d5","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Vwi3DZuohf6VXxZxeDUq3e","type":"tool_result","content":"<system-reminder>This memory is 48 days old. Memories are point-in-time observations, not live state — claims about code behavior or file:line citations may be outdated. Verify against current code before asserting as fact.</system-reminder>\n1\t---\n2\tname: alpen-parallel-development\n3\tdescription: Alpen (fun/alpen) gets substantial parallel work landed on origin/main outside this session — check for divergence before assuming a clean push\n4\tmetadata: \n5\t  node_type: memory\n6\t  type: project\n7\t  modified: 2026-08-07T16:04:04.695Z\n8\t  originSessionId: 0b0b9770-3ca7-4e24-ac68-7442a7ca40fa\n9\t---\n10\t\n11\tAlpen's `main.js`/`config.js`/`props.js`/`riderModel.js`/`terrain.js` are being actively developed in parallel by other sessions/PRs, not just this one. On 2026-08-07, local work (terrain zone model + guide line + 3D model imports, [[alpen-debug-workflow]]) had diverged from `origin/main` by 3 unrelated PRs (flank fluting/far-field snow/cloth rig/butter tricks/loading bar; wildlife/lit gates/geology/a touchdown-tunnel physics fix; the park+rails feature's removal) touching the exact same five files.\n12\t\n13\t**Why:** Same repo, same small set of hot files, worked on from multiple sessions/PRs without coordination between them.\n14\t\n15\t**How to apply:** Before starting nontrivial Alpen terrain/physics/prop work in a fresh session, `git fetch origin main` and check `git status --short --branch` for `behind` — don't assume local `main` is caught up. Before a `git push`, re-fetch and re-check even if it was clean at session start (a merge earlier in the session doesn't mean the remote stayed still). If a conflict surfaces: `git merge-tree main origin/main` is a safe read-only conflict preview (needs `dangerouslyDisableSandbox` for its temp file). Dispatch Explore agents at the specific conflicting files/commit range rather than the whole diff — but verify their claims against the actual current file content before trusting them for merge decisions; one agent's report here confidently described a `debug().gates` field that turned out not to exist anywhere in either branch.\n16\t"}]},"uuid":"f82c3e34-16a5-4787-a77f-42f8a96b1870","timestamp":"2026-09-24T19:49:48.544Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/vojta/.claude/projects/-Users-vojta-Dev-protocodus-github-io/memory/alpen-parallel-development.md","content":"---\nname: alpen-parallel-development\ndescription: Alpen (fun/alpen) gets substantial parallel work landed on origin/main outside this session — check for divergence before assuming a clean push\nmetadata: \n  node_type: memory\n  type: project\n  modified: 2026-08-07T16:04:04.695Z\n  originSessionId: 0b0b9770-3ca7-4e24-ac68-7442a7ca40fa\n---\n\nAlpen's `main.js`/`config.js`/`props.js`/`riderModel.js`/`terrain.js` are being actively developed in parallel by other sessions/PRs, not just this one. On 2026-08-07, local work (terrain zone model + guide line + 3D model imports, [[alpen-debug-workflow]]) had diverged from `origin/main` by 3 unrelated PRs (flank fluting/far-field snow/cloth rig/butter tricks/loading bar; wildlife/lit gates/geology/a touchdown-tunnel physics fix; the park+rails feature's removal) touching the exact same five files.\n\n**Why:** Same repo, same small set of hot files, worked on from multiple sessions/PRs without coordination between them.\n\n**How to apply:** Before starting nontrivial Alpen terrain/physics/prop work in a fresh session, `git fetch origin main` and check `git status --short --branch` for `behind` — don't assume local `main` is caught up. Before a `git push`, re-fetch and re-check even if it was clean at session start (a merge earlier in the session doesn't mean the remote stayed still). If a conflict surfaces: `git merge-tree main origin/main` is a safe read-only conflict preview (needs `dangerouslyDisableSandbox` for its temp file). Dispatch Explore agents at the specific conflicting files/commit range rather than the whole diff — but verify their claims against the actual current file content before trusting them for merge decisions; one agent's report here confidently described a `debug().gates` field that turned out not to exist anywhere in either branch.\n","numLines":16,"startLine":1,"totalLines":16}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"50110d64-0343-4487-862c-4286d12a4614","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/Users/vojta/Dev/protocodus.github.io/fun/alpen","sessionId":"f31fbc8b-fac8-4283-8f36-bb5424b19347","version":"2.1.281","gitBranch":"main","slug":"enchanted-prancing-stroustrup"}
