{"parentUuid":"071893f3-f957-46d6-8320-963049d96db8","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"c41cd6de-57c3-441a-96f7-ed621873bfe7","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01RTcudNHBz4zgX4PxDSuWFU","type":"tool_result","content":"73:const rawBoot = window.__alpenBoot || { step() {}, giveUp() {} };\n1693:   Set one at a time from the console — `__alpen.flicker.noShadow = true` —\n1749:window.__alpen = {\n1749:window.__alpen = {\n1750-  flicker: flickerProbe,\n1751-  game, rider, camera, chase, world, weather, scene, sky, terrain, props, retro, renderer,\n1752-  // `model` is on here for one reason: the rider's drawn orientation is\n1753-  // derived from the physics yaw and has been wrong before — mirrored about\n1754-  // the fall line, which is invisible going straight and 180° out in a carve.\n1755-  // Without a handle on it that can only be checked by eye, and it is exactly\n1756-  // the class of bug an eye slides over.\n1757-  wildlife, audio, trail, huts, model,\n1758-  /* And the handles needed to *drive* the game from here rather than only\n1759-     read it. `input` is the live control state, so a carve can be held from\n1760-     the console; the three particle systems are the parts of the picture\n1761-     whose output cannot be judged from a still frame taken at whatever moment\n1762-     the loop happened to be in. Between them the plume a committed turn\n1763-     throws can be produced deliberately and then looked at. */\n1764-  input, spray, snowfall, streaks,\n1765-  /* And the block that decides how everything on the mountain is lit. It is\n1766-     the one shared piece of state with no other handle on it: the sun, the\n1767-     fog curtain, the cloud deck and its shadow, and the terrain's own baked\n1768-     horizon all arrive through here, so a question of the form \"which of\n1769-     these is putting that on the wall\" can only be answered by switching\n1770-     them off one at a time. `mountainLife` is here for the same reason —\n1771-     its riders are the only things on the hill that move under their own\n1772-     steam, and a pose that is wrong is a pose you have to be able to stop. */\n1773-  shading, mountainLife,\n1774-  config: { RENDER, RIDER, SCORE, PROPS, GRADE },\n1775-  debug: () => ({\n1776-    mode: game.mode,\n1777-    speed: +(rider.speed * 3.6).toFixed(1),\n1778-    flow: +game.flow.toFixed(3),\n1779-    flowHold: +game.flowHold.toFixed(2),\n1780-    combo: game.combo,\n1781-    pos: [rider.pos.x, rider.pos.y, rider.pos.z].map((v) => +v.toFixed(1)),\n1782-    state: rider.state,\n1783-    grounded: rider.grounded,\n1784-    switchStance: rider.switchStance,\n1785-    boardForward: +rider.boardForward.toFixed(2),\n1786-    upCourse: rider.vel.z > 0.05,\n1787-    airTime: +rider.airTime.toFixed(2),\n1788-    climbRate: +rider.climbRate.toFixed(2),\n1789-    edge: +(rider.edge || 0).toFixed(2),","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"3d488259-f381-4de4-9933-6bd798f6aaa7","timestamp":"2026-09-24T19:57:25.257Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"73:const rawBoot = window.__alpenBoot || { step() {}, giveUp() {} };\n1693:   Set one at a time from the console — `__alpen.flicker.noShadow = true` —\n1749:window.__alpen = {\n1749:window.__alpen = {\n1750-  flicker: flickerProbe,\n1751-  game, rider, camera, chase, world, weather, scene, sky, terrain, props, retro, renderer,\n1752-  // `model` is on here for one reason: the rider's drawn orientation is\n1753-  // derived from the physics yaw and has been wrong before — mirrored about\n1754-  // the fall line, which is invisible going straight and 180° out in a carve.\n1755-  // Without a handle on it that can only be checked by eye, and it is exactly\n1756-  // the class of bug an eye slides over.\n1757-  wildlife, audio, trail, huts, model,\n1758-  /* And the handles needed to *drive* the game from here rather than only\n1759-     read it. `input` is the live control state, so a carve can be held from\n1760-     the console; the three particle systems are the parts of the picture\n1761-     whose output cannot be judged from a still frame taken at whatever moment\n1762-     the loop happened to be in. Between them the plume a committed turn\n1763-     throws can be produced deliberately and then looked at. */\n1764-  input, spray, snowfall, streaks,\n1765-  /* And the block that decides how everything on the mountain is lit. It is\n1766-     the one shared piece of state with no other handle on it: the sun, the\n1767-     fog curtain, the cloud deck and its shadow, and the terrain's own baked\n1768-     horizon all arrive through here, so a question of the form \"which of\n1769-     these is putting that on the wall\" can only be answered by switching\n1770-     them off one at a time. `mountainLife` is here for the same reason —\n1771-     its riders are the only things on the hill that move under their own\n1772-     steam, and a pose that is wrong is a pose you have to be able to stop. */\n1773-  shading, mountainLife,\n1774-  config: { RENDER, RIDER, SCORE, PROPS, GRADE },\n1775-  debug: () => ({\n1776-    mode: game.mode,\n1777-    speed: +(rider.speed * 3.6).toFixed(1),\n1778-    flow: +game.flow.toFixed(3),\n1779-    flowHold: +game.flowHold.toFixed(2),\n1780-    combo: game.combo,\n1781-    pos: [rider.pos.x, rider.pos.y, rider.pos.z].map((v) => +v.toFixed(1)),\n1782-    state: rider.state,\n1783-    grounded: rider.grounded,\n1784-    switchStance: rider.switchStance,\n1785-    boardForward: +rider.boardForward.toFixed(2),\n1786-    upCourse: rider.vel.z > 0.05,\n1787-    airTime: +rider.airTime.toFixed(2),\n1788-    climbRate: +rider.climbRate.toFixed(2),\n1789-    edge: +(rider.edge || 0).toFixed(2),","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"071893f3-f957-46d6-8320-963049d96db8","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/Users/vojta/Dev/protocodus.github.io/fun/alpen","sessionId":"f31fbc8b-fac8-4283-8f36-bb5424