{"parentUuid":"0697bca2-bcb9-488d-8e7f-0edc345baa5f","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"c41cd6de-57c3-441a-96f7-ed621873bfe7","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_018yeuje4YUr5ETz352d9RMQ","type":"tool_result","content":"585:    // W is a powered tuck. This is a speed floor rather than a\n586-    // one-off force: snow friction, a traverse, or an extreme drag value can\n587-    // never quietly create another terminal velocity. Gravity and clean\n588-    // terrain can still add more than the floor, so the mountain remains part\n589-    // of the acceleration instead of being overwritten by it.\n590-    /* …and how hard, which is what the flow meter is spent on. `flowDrive`\n591-       is written once a step by `stepFlow` in main.js: a full meter is the\n592-       whole powered tuck this has always been, an empty one is a third of\n593-       it. The floor still cannot create a second terminal velocity — it is\n594-       still a floor, and gravity and a clean line still beat it — but the\n595-       speed it guarantees is now something the run has to have earned. */\n596-    const drive = 0.34 + 0.66 * Math.min(1, Math.max(0, this.flowDrive));\n597-\n598-    // Gravity, resolved on the tangent. This is the whole engine: steep is\n599-    // fast, banked is slow, and neither needed a special case.","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"2bb2bc91-2244-4f90-8218-af2a726b6d1d","timestamp":"2026-09-24T20:09:34.937Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"585:    // W is a powered tuck. This is a speed floor rather than a\n586-    // one-off force: snow friction, a traverse, or an extreme drag value can\n587-    // never quietly create another terminal velocity. Gravity and clean\n588-    // terrain can still add more than the floor, so the mountain remains part\n589-    // of the acceleration instead of being overwritten by it.\n590-    /* …and how hard, which is what the flow meter is spent on. `flowDrive`\n591-       is written once a step by `stepFlow` in main.js: a full meter is the\n592-       whole powered tuck this has always been, an empty one is a third of\n593-       it. The floor still cannot create a second terminal velocity — it is\n594-       still a floor, and gravity and a clean line still beat it — but the\n595-       speed it guarantees is now something the run has to have earned. */\n596-    const drive = 0.34 + 0.66 * Math.min(1, Math.max(0, this.flowDrive));\n597-\n598-    // Gravity, resolved on the tangent. This is the whole engine: steep is\n599-    // fast, banked is slow, and neither needed a special case.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"0697bca2-bcb9-488d-8e7f-0edc345baa5f","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/Users/vojta/Dev/protocodus.github.io/fun/alpen","sessionId":"f31fbc8b-fac8-4283-8f36-bb5424b19347","version":"2.1.281","gitBranch":"main","slug":"enchanted-prancing-stroustrup"}
