{"parentUuid":"7f6e71bc-3714-4eb8-8d25-c612733257b1","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfNtiD9HidyTVFj8jBntY","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01VTA1wg9Qu2sTq96J6BAbsg","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/vojta/Dev/protocodus.github.io && git log -5 --format='%s%n%b---' | head -40","description":"Read recent commit messages for style"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2073,"cache_read_input_tokens":561810,"output_tokens":317,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":197},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2073,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":317,"cache_read_input_tokens":561810,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2073,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2073},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[{"type":"thinking_dropped","path":"messages.2.content.0","reason":"prefix_binding_mismatch"}],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01VTA1wg9Qu2sTq96J6BAbsg":{"command":"cd /Users/vojta/Dev/protocodus.github.io && git log -5 --format='%s%n%b---' | head -40","description":"Read recent commit messages for style"}},"apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CfNthvVAka8u2HmnJZbrx","type":"assistant","uuid":"0e5f437d-ee5e-426c-9c34-34e4f5c5bbc6","timestamp":"2026-09-24T20:26:04.379Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"max","perTurnEffort":"max","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/private/tmp/claude-501/c1tree/fun/alpen","sessionId":"f31fbc8b-fac8-4283-8f36-bb5424b19347","version":"2.1.281","gitBranch":"main","slug":"enchanted-prancing-stroustrup"}
{"parentUuid":"0e5f437d-ee5e-426c-9c34-34e4f5c5bbc6","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"c41cd6de-57c3-441a-96f7-ed621873bfe7","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01VTA1wg9Qu2sTq96J6BAbsg","type":"tool_result","content":"feat(alpen): lay the sky photos out at their own scale; rebuild clouds and aurora\n- The sunrise, sunset and night plates are 16:9 photographs, not 360°\n  panoramas, but were wrapped round the whole ring: every summit drawn at\n  twice the size the photo resolves, with a seam uphill. They are now laid\n  across half the ring at their own aspect, mirrored for the rest, with\n  their ridge stood where the day panorama's is. Magnified plates are\n  rebuilt with a Catmull-Rom kernel (five fetches) instead of bilinear.\n- The relief shell drew flat grey cones in front of the photographs at the\n  vanishing point. It now sinks away as a plate is revealed and remains the\n  fallback while plates load or if they fail; it is lit by the real key and\n  fill for that case.\n- Cirrus was stretched hash noise that read as horizontal scan lines; it is\n  now warped, jet-aligned strands with clear patches, from a small cloud\n  texture baked at boot (~5 ms). Cloud-deck cells get torn edges and lumpy\n  tops above the band where the fog copy of the sky meets it.\n- The aurora was isotropic blobs; it is now curtains with a sharp wandering\n  lower edge and vertical rays, at the same four fetches.\n\nFixed-camera A/B against the previous build: CPU per frame unchanged, GPU\np50 within run-to-run noise (day 9.35 vs 9.49 ms, night 9.56 vs 9.38 ms).\ngraphics-check covers the plate layouts and the relief's retirement.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nEntire-Checkpoint: 0a433428e8b2\n---\nfeat(alpen): make the flow multiplier earned by tricks, not by riding\nMeasured with the real rider on three seeded mountains, steering down the\ngroomed line filled the meter in about nine seconds and held the top x12\nmultiplier for ~90% of a run. A wipeout's cost was back within seconds, and\nMAX FLOW fired on every drop-in, so the multiplier said nothing about how a\nrun was going.\n\nThe meter rules move out of main.js into flow.js, where node can test them:\n- clean, fast riding settles at a cruise level (x3) and fills nothing above;\n- tricks, butters and cocoa stops fill the rest and hold it for 4 s of\n  riding, after which the surplus relaxes back towards cruise;\n- gates pay a third of the meter they did and never hold it (every gate\n  spans the piste, so a run of them is staying on it, not a trick);\n- a wipeout still takes 55% and now also ends the hold.","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"f9d89910-cb2e-4bd0-8d3b-09dff5a662f9","timestamp":"2026-09-24T20:26:04.719Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"feat(alpen): lay the sky photos out at their own scale; rebuild clouds and aurora\n- The sunrise, sunset and night plates are 16:9 photographs, not 360°\n  panoramas, but were wrapped round the whole ring: every summit drawn at\n  twice the size the photo resolves, with a seam uphill. They are now laid\n  across half the ring at their own aspect, mirrored for the rest, with\n  their ridge stood where the day panorama's is. Magnified plates are\n  rebuilt with a Catmull-Rom kernel (five fetches) instead of bilinear.\n- The relief shell drew flat grey cones in front of the photographs at the\n  vanishing point. It now sinks away as a plate is revealed and remains the\n  fallback while plates load or if they fail; it is lit by the real key and\n  fill for that case.\n- Cirrus was stretched hash noise that read as horizontal scan lines; it is\n  now warped, jet-aligned strands with clear patches, from a small cloud\n  texture baked at boot (~5 ms). Cloud-deck cells get torn edges and lumpy\n  tops above the band where the fog copy of the sky meets it.\n- The aurora was isotropic blobs; it is now curtains with a sharp wandering\n  lower edge and vertical rays, at the same four fetches.\n\nFixed-camera A/B against the previous build: CPU per frame unchanged, GPU\np50 within run-to-run noise (day 9.35 vs 9.49 ms, night 9.56 vs 9.38 ms).\ngraphics-check covers the plate layouts and the relief's retirement.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nEntire-Checkpoint: 0a433428e8b2\n---\nfeat(alpen): make the flow multiplier earned by tricks, not by riding\nMeasured with the real rider on three seeded mountains, steering down the\ngroomed line filled the meter in about nine seconds and held the top x12\nmultiplier for ~90% of a run. A wipeout's cost was back within seconds, and\nMAX FLOW fired on every drop-in, so the multiplier said nothing about how a\nrun was going.\n\nThe meter rules move out of main.js into flow.js, where node can test them:\n- clean, fast riding settles at a cruise level (x3) and fills nothing above;\n- tricks, butters and cocoa stops fill the rest and hold it for 4 s of\n  riding, after which the surplus relaxes back towards cruise;\n- gates pay a third of the meter they did and never hold it (every gate\n  spans the piste, so a run of them is staying on it, not a trick);\n- a wipeout still takes 55% and now also ends the hold.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"0e5f437d-ee5e-426c-9c34-34e4f5c5bbc6","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/Users/vojta/Dev/protocodus.github.io","sessionId":"f31fbc8b-fac8-4283-8f36-bb5424b19347","version":"2.1.281","gitBranch":"main","slug":"enchanted-prancing-stroustrup"}
